    "kSide": 0.8,
    "kWild": 0.02,
    "kWildSpin": 0.6,
    "wildAxisMaxDeg": 25,
    "warmChargePerTurn": 4,
    "bombLiftMetres": 0.25,
    "_powerEase": "The exponent of the ease out curve, in sixteenths: 21/16 = 1.3125. At that exponent the top 20 percent of a player's effort buys the last 12.1 percent of power, which is what DESIGN 7.2 asks for. It is stated in sixteenths because Math.pow is not bit reproducible across engines and core computes it with four square roots instead.",
    "_k": "kBack, kTop, kSide and kWildSpin are MULTIPLES OF THE NATURAL ROLLING RATE (launch speed divided by radius), so they are scale free: 1.0 of top spin is exactly the spin a marble of that size would have if it were rolling at that speed. Tuned in K1 against the sticking scenario."
  },

